From 834d99c2c8b809fb36fbdec3b6d2df834c546777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:14:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: rkisp2: Document the AWB gain width

The comment of struct rkisp2_isp_awb_gains gives a range of 0 to 63 and
leaves the upper two bits open. The colour gain registers of the RV1126
ISP 2.0 hold 10 bits, so gains from 4 upwards wrap around, which was
measured with gains of 10, 20 and 38 that act as 2, 0 and 2.

State the range of the ISP 2.0 and that the other versions are
unverified.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 include/uapi/linux/media/rockchip/rkisp2-config.h | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

--- a/include/uapi/linux/media/rockchip/rkisp2-config.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/media/rockchip/rkisp2-config.h
@@ -254,12 +254,11 @@ struct rkisp2_isp_bls_fixed_val {
  * struct rkisp2_isp_awb_gains - Auto white balance gain in the ISP block
  *
  * All fields in this struct are 16 bit, where:
- * 0x100h = 1, unsigned integer value, range 0 to 63 with 8 bit fractional part.
+ * 0x100h = 1, unsigned integer value with 8 bit fractional part.
  *
- * This leaves the upper two msb unaccounted for; it is unknown if these are
- * unused or misdocumented.
- *
- * TODO investigate the upper two bits
+ * The ISP 2.0 of the RV1126 implements only the lower 10 bits, so its gains
+ * range from 0 to 3.996 and larger values wrap around. The width on the other
+ * ISP versions is unknown.
  *
  * @r: gain value for red component.
  * @gr: gain value for green component in red line.
